289	  // server") is deliberately created `active: false` — every plain
290	  // `where: { active: true }` catalog/resize-picker/marketing query in this
291	  // codebase (30+ call sites, none scoped to a single order or customer) must
292	  // never surface it as a generically pickable tile. But it must still be a
293	  // valid target for the ONE order that just built it, so `sortOrder` — the
294	  // existing marker reserved for exactly this row shape — is accepted here as an
295	  // alternative to `active`. No other code path needs this carve-out: renewals
296	  // (lib/renewal-charge.ts) never check `active` at all, and the resize-target
297	  // picker's own `where: { active: true }` query correctly keeps a custom plan
298	  // out of every OTHER customer's upgrade options with no change needed there.
299	  const planPurchasable = !!plan?.active || plan?.sortOrder === CUSTOM_PLAN_SORT_ORDER;
